WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.624 --> 00:00:03.626
That night the moon shone bright and full.

2
00:00:03.646 --> 00:00:05.187
Ben headed over to Monster Academy early.

3
00:00:05.207 --> 00:00:07.509
"What a fantastic night," he said to himself.

4
00:00:30.436 --> 00:00:34.437
"There will be great music, great food, and a whole night with Winnie!"

5
00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:43.520
At school Ben peeked into the gym to see if Winnie and the others were still working on

6
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.420
the decorations.

7
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.501
"Wow!" he burst out.

8
00:00:48.001 --> 00:00:53.602
Silky spider webs shimmered from the ceiling, and eerie lights cast spooky shadows around the room.

9
00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:59.444
Onstage the Boneyard Brass Band was setting up their equipment.

10
00:01:01.132 --> 00:01:05.695
One skeleton tuned a trumpet, while another tapped a tune on his own rib cage.

11
00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:08.936
"Winnie?" Ben called.

12
00:01:10.237 --> 00:01:14.920
The skeletons looked up, but there was no sign of Winnie or anyone else from the dance committee.

13
00:01:17.301 --> 00:01:18.822
Ben stepped out into the hallway.

14
00:01:23.284 --> 00:01:25.185
Ben!" Waldo Wizz called.

15
00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:27.086
"You're here early."

16
00:01:27.106 --> 00:01:29.888
"Yeah." Ben shrugged.

17
00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:32.789
"Winnie's here already, decorating the gym.

18
00:01:33.529 --> 00:01:34.990
I thought I'd come early to help her."

19
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.772
"I think she finished decorating," Waldo reported.

20
00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:42.473
"A bunch of girls just went upstairs to change into their dresses.

21
00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:48.116
I've got nothing to do now, so I was going to check on my latest magic experiment.

22
00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:49.476
Want to see it?"

23
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.057
"Sure," said Ben.

24
00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:55.639
"It's in the science lab, and it's top secret."

25
00:01:56.259 --> 00:01:57.880
Waldo led the way to the lab.

26
00:02:01.516 --> 00:02:03.037
"You can't tell anyone about it."

27
00:02:04.118 --> 00:02:05.219
Ben held up a hand.

28
00:02:05.239 --> 00:02:07.221
"I promise, Waldo."

29
00:02:08.422 --> 00:02:12.025
As they turned a corner, Waldo bumped into a large purple blob.

30
00:02:12.825 --> 00:02:14.547
His glasses flew off his face.

31
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:21.452
"Oh!" Waldo fumbled for them on the floor and then put them back on.

32
00:02:21.472 --> 00:02:24.014
"Hi, Jen."

33
00:02:24.034 --> 00:02:28.278
"Sorry about that, Waldo," said the blob.

34
00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:33.433
"You haven't seen a, um, human around here, have you?"

35
00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.095
"A human?"

36
00:02:35.615 --> 00:02:36.395
echoed Waldo.

37
00:02:36.415 --> 00:02:41.179
"He's my date," said Jen awkwardly.

38
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.702
Ben wasn't sure, but the purple blob appeared to be blushing.

39
00:02:45.722 --> 00:02:50.705
"I left him alone while I got ready upstairs with the witches.

40
00:02:52.927 --> 00:02:54.308
Now I can't find him."

41
00:02:54.328 --> 00:02:58.271
"We haven't seen him," Waldo said to Jen.

42
00:02:58.291 --> 00:03:01.544
"If we do, though, we'll let him know you're looking for him."

43
00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:08.226
"He's a little freaked out by Monster Academy," said the blob, jiggling as she talked.

44
00:03:08.246 --> 00:03:11.567
"I don't understand humans sometimes."

45
00:03:11.587 --> 00:03:15.689
"Yeah, humans are weird," agreed Waldo.

46
00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:17.629
"We'll keep an eye out for him."

47
00:03:18.869 --> 00:03:20.250
"Thanks, Waldo."

48
00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:27.352
Jen moved past Waldo and Ben, and glided down the hallway, leaving behind a shiny trail of slime.

49
00:03:28.936 --> 00:03:32.459
"I didn't know there'd be a human at the Monster Mash," said Waldo.

50
00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:34.921
"Me neither," said Ben.

51
00:03:35.861 --> 00:03:36.542
He shivered.

52
00:03:36.562 --> 00:03:41.846
"Creepy!" Ben and Waldo entered the science lab.

53
00:03:42.907 --> 00:03:45.569
Inside, Waldo gasped.

54
00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:48.411
A strange purple fog filled the room.

55
00:03:50.232 --> 00:03:54.536
Through the fog Ben could see test tubes and rubber hoses on a counter in the back.

56
00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.441
Near them a small appliance that looked like a pressure cooker beeped noisily.

57
00:04:00.642 --> 00:04:02.402
Waldo rushed to the back of the lab.

58
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:07.204
He quickly flipped a switch on the appliance, and the beeping stopped.

59
00:04:08.184 --> 00:04:12.565
Ben floated over and saw that the hoses were all connected to the small appliance.

60
00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:16.947
"I'm trying to make a talk potion," Waldo explained.

61
00:04:16.967 --> 00:04:20.988
"Whoever drinks the potion will talk and talk and talk."

62
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.602
"Why would anyone want to drink a talk potion?"

63
00:04:26.062 --> 00:04:26.643
asked Ben.

64
00:04:26.663 --> 00:04:30.286
"It's mostly for shy people," Waldo explained.

65
00:04:30.306 --> 00:04:34.689
"But His cheeks were bright pink.

66
00:04:34.709 --> 00:04:38.553
"But it looks like somebody pulled all the hoses off the test tubes!

67
00:04:39.413 --> 00:04:40.354
Who would do that?"

68
00:04:40.374 --> 00:04:42.436
"Shy people?"

69
00:04:43.076 --> 00:04:43.657
said Ben.

70
00:04:44.838 --> 00:04:46.439
Waldo gave Ben a funny look.

71
00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.582
"Why would shy people try to ruin my potion?"

72
00:04:51.863 --> 00:04:54.117
"No, I mean Ben tried to explain.

73
00:04:54.137 --> 00:04:57.558
"You said this talk potion is for shy people.

74
00:04:58.418 --> 00:05:01.120
So I was asking why shy people would need it."

75
00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.941
"Oh, right," said Waldo.

76
00:05:06.502 --> 00:05:08.943
He began putting the hoses back on the test tubes.

77
00:05:08.963 --> 00:05:12.985
"Well, usually shy people don't know what to talk about.

78
00:05:14.105 --> 00:05:16.906
But if they drink my potion, they'll have plenty to talk about.

79
00:05:18.047 --> 00:05:20.848
Police could also use it on suspects who are refusing to talk."

80
00:05:23.472 --> 00:05:25.153
"Oh, I see," said Ben.

81
00:05:26.654 --> 00:05:32.357
Though, knowing Waldo, Ben had a feeling that the potion might not work exactly as Waldo had described.

82
00:05:32.377 --> 00:05:35.219
"Is everything okay?"

83
00:05:36.379 --> 00:05:42.263
"I think so By now the purple fog in the room was beginning to clear.

84
00:05:43.043 --> 00:05:46.205
Ben could see it disappearing into an air vent in the ceiling.

85
00:05:49.206 --> 00:05:51.808
Boom! A sound came from the front of the room.

86
00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.181
"What was that?"

87
00:05:53.581 --> 00:05:54.222
Ben asked.

88
00:05:55.563 --> 00:05:57.724
Waldo was still busy fixing his equipment.

89
00:05:57.744 --> 00:06:02.909
"There!" he said triumphantly as the appliance began to hum.

90
00:06:05.371 --> 00:06:07.773
Ben saw that the door to the lab was now shut.

91
00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:12.737
He hurried over and tried the handle.

92
00:06:12.757 --> 00:06:17.120
"Uh, Waldo he said nervously.

93
00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.043
"I think we're locked in here."

94
00:06:20.063 --> 00:06:23.474
"Huh?" Waldo finally looked up.

95
00:06:24.336 --> 00:06:29.583
"What?" Ben tried the handle again, but the door still wouldn't budge.

96
00:06:29.603 --> 00:06:33.409
"I mean that someone locked us in the science lab.

97
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.172
We can't get out!"
